  "verbalization": "Vinblastine is linked to MDA-MB-361 through a series of molecular interactions, with the core mechanism involving the target compound 3-[2-[4-[5-[2-(2,3-Dihydroxyphenyl)ethyl]-2-hydroxyphenoxy]phenyl]ethyl]benzene-1,2-diol. This compound is identified as a target of vinblastine and is itself a target of multiple cell lines, including MDA-MB-361. The evidence suggests that vinblastine exerts its effects by binding to and inhibiting the activity of this target compound, which in turn affects the growth and survival of MDA-MB-361 cells. The consistent presence of this target compound in multiple cell lines, coupled with the direct link between vinblastine and MDA-MB-361, supports a mechanism of action that involves the inhibition of a shared molecular target. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for vinblastine in targeting a common molecular pathway in breast cancer cells, emphasizing its relevance in cancer therapy.",
